To generate the assert statement for the given comment, we need to ensure that for each index `i` from the given `index` to the old size minus one, either both the current and old elements at `i+1` are null, or the current element at `i+1` equals the old element at `i`.

Here's how we can express this in an assert statement:

1. We need to compare the elements at positions `i+1` before and after the insertion.
2. We need to ensure that the comparison holds for all valid indices `i` from `index` to `size-1` (before the insertion).

Given the constraints and the available methods, we can use the `get` method to retrieve elements at specific indices.

Here is the assert statement:

<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i+1)) == null) || this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

This assert statement ensures that for each index `i` in the specified range, either both the current and old elements at `i+1` are null, or the current element at `i+1` equals the old element at `i`.--------------------<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (\this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i+1)) == null) || \this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>--------------------<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (\old(this.get(i+1)) == null && this.get(i+1) == null) || this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>--------------------